    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d209">

                <pb facs="0211" n="201" xml:id="pg201"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811D.0144/5: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-08T20:00:00+09:00">July 8, 1941—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 8—12:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>958. Department’s 376, July 5, 9 p.m.<anchor n="77" xml:id="d209-f1"/> I
                    reemphasized today personally to the Minister for Foreign Affairs the serious
                    view taken by the Government of the United States of the unauthorized flights of
                    Japanese planes over the Island of Guam and urgently requested that the Foreign
                    Office expedite its reply to my previous representations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
